    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d105">

                <pb facs="0231" n="113" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg113"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.75/14: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Goold</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-25T13:00:00+02:00">May 25, 1929—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 25—10:57 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>39. Your telegram No. 26, May 18, 6 p.m.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d105-f1"/> An
                    adjudication for the telephone concession is to be held on June 5th. Minister of
                    Communications has indicated that he would like local agent to make firm<anchor
                        n="33" xml:id="d105-f2"/> offer, although company’s ideas have been
                    altogether different from those of government. Local agent has telegraphed to
                    London requesting that authorized agent be sent at once.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Goold</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d105-f1" n="32" xml:id="d105-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d105-f2" n="33" xml:id="d105-f2-content">
                <p>i. e., the International Telephone and Telegraph Corporation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
